From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: a pause stops the picture where the sound stops

A pause the resume is not prepared behind (an MVC film, a struggling
source) paused the audio stream with the clock. Pausing the only stream
flushes the engine and the sink, so the audio already queued there, some
170 ms on TrueHD, was never heard; the resume went on after it, found
the audio that far ahead of the frozen clock and filled the gap with
silence: an audible cut after every pause.

Stop feeding the audio at once instead and leave the stream running, so
the engine plays out what it holds. The sink reports where the audio
being heard is, from the end of what was written and its delay now; once
that holds still the queue has played out, and the clock and the picture
are stopped there and the stream paused with nothing left to flush,
within a second at most. A resume before then cancels the pending stop;
a flush stops the clock at once. The picture freezes that much after the
key, and the resume continues the sound exactly where it stopped.

Shared code: the clock and the pause are CVideoPlayer's, and the audio
position is the sink's; the touch is one accessor on the audio player
interface and the deferral itself.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
